---
status: approved
intent: >
  Build the /learn section shell: its layout, the shared private template that
  renders one copy record, the index page and the six page routes, each wiring
  its record into the metadata helper and the structured-data builder.
---

## Commitments

1. **Layout composition.** The /learn layout renders: skip link, the site TopBar (sticky), `<main id="main">`, the site Footer. No docs sidebar, no /brain palette or footer. It is not the docs layout (docsRegistry renders package markdown only) and not the /brain layout.

2. **Private template components** under the section's private components folder, one default export per file: `LearnArticle` (orchestrator), `LearnBreadcrumb`, `LearnHeader`, `LearnSection`, `ComparisonTable`, `FaqList`, `RelatedLinks`. They reuse `src/components` (`CodeBlock`, `Callout`, `DocMeta` or a learn variant, see open question 1) and the `.docs-body` prose class from `globals.css`. No new CSS custom properties, typefaces, colours, spacing values or callout styles.

3. **Fixed render order inside `<article>`.** `LearnBreadcrumb` → `LearnHeader` (H1, then the answer/definition paragraph immediately as the next sibling, then the date/author line) → `LearnSection`[] (H2 with `id`) → `ComparisonTable` (only when the record has rows) → `FaqList` (only when the record has FAQ items) → `RelatedLinks`. Copy cannot reorder or insert blocks. Nothing renders between the H1 and the answer paragraph.

4. **Server-only tree.** No `'use client'` anywhere under `src/app/learn/`. Every word of the answer, sections, table, FAQ and related links is in the static export HTML. Interactive pieces reused from `src/components` (e.g. CodeBlock's copy button) may be client islands but carry no page copy.

5. **One record in, one pass.** Each page route imports its copy record from `src/data/learn/<pageKey>` (via the roster) and passes the same object to `LearnArticle`, to `buildPageMetadata` (title, description, canonical, own og:image, `alternates.types` for `text/markdown` and `application/atom+xml`) and to the structured-data builders. Route files contain no literal copy strings. `generateMetadata`/`metadata` comes only from the helper.

6. **Visible date and author.** `<time dateTime="YYYY-MM-DD">` showing the page's `modified` date from `listSitePages` (the git date of its copy module); omitted when absent, never build-stamped. Author/publisher text is "Lowmeadow LLC"; no person name, no personal link.

7. **Breadcrumb.** The visible trail renders `listSitePages`' `breadcrumb` entry for the page (Home → learn → page title; index: Home → learn). The `BreadcrumbList` record is built from that same entry. Visible labels and record `name`s identical; same item count.

8. **Records per page** (via `src/service/structuredData`, emitted by `src/components/JsonLd`, serializer escapes `<` as `<`):
   - Every /learn page incl. the index: `BreadcrumbList`.
   - Six answer pages: `Article` — `headline` = H1, `description`, `url`/`mainEntityOfPage` = canonical with trailing slash, `dateModified` (and `datePublished`) from `listSitePages` only when present, `author` and `publisher` = `{ "@id": "https://aidemd.dev/#organization" }`, `isPartOf` = `{ "@id": "https://aidemd.dev/#website" }` by reference. No inline Organization, no Person. (Index record type: open question 3.)
   - intent-driven-engineering and open-source-agentic-sdlc-framework only: `FAQPage` with `mainEntity: Question[]` whose `name`/`acceptedAnswer.text` are the exact strings `FaqList` renders, same order, same count; and `DefinedTerm` (in a `DefinedTermSet` where there are several) whose `name`/`description` are the exact glossary strings rendered, each `url` = canonical + `#<termAnchor>`.

9. **Stable anchors.** Every section H2 and every glossary term carries an `id` taken from the copy record (not derived from heading text at render time), so a copy edit to a heading does not break inbound anchor links.

10. **Index page.** Lists the six pages from the roster in roster order (research priority: intent-driven-engineering, spec-driven-vs-intent-driven-development, spec-kit-alternatives, claude-code-subagents-pipeline, mcp-server-for-development-workflow, open-source-agentic-sdlc-framework), each with title and description from its record. Same layout and prose styles; no lastModified.

11. **Related links.** Each page's `RelatedLinks` renders the record's related list: sibling /learn pages, docs routes, /observer. The subagents-pipeline page links `/docs/hooks/` and `/observer/`. All internal hrefs carry trailing slashes.

12. **No review-state branch.** No component or route reads the record's draft marker to hide, noindex, exclude from the roster/sitemap/feed, or alter rendering. No `robots: { index: false }` on any /learn page.

13. **Comparison tables.** `ComparisonTable` renders a semantic `<table>` (thead/tbody, `scope` on header cells) styled by docs prose; every competitor number cell renders its as-of date from the record.

14. **Template additions (plan 2026-11-27).** Beyond the seven parts in #2, the private template has `LearnHeader/LearnByline` (the slim date/author line), `LearnSection/LearnBlock` and `LearnSection/GlossaryList`, `LearnIndexList` (the index list) and `shared/RichTextRuns` (inline runs: internal links via next/link, external via `<a>`). All server components; `LearnBlock` is async only to highlight code with `@/lib/shiki` and `aide-theme` through `@/components/CodeBlock`.

15. **Fixed template words.** The only words the template shows that are not in a page's record are `templateLabels` from `@/data/learn/templateLabels` (`faqHeading` "Frequently asked questions" with id `faq`, `relatedHeading` "Related" with id `related`, `asOfPrefix` "as of", `updatedLabel` "Updated") and the author `siteIdentity.name`. The ids `faq` and `related` are reserved: no section or glossary id may use them.

16. **Exact renderings shared with the markdown copy.** Byline: `Updated <time dateTime="YYYY-MM-DD">YYYY-MM-DD</time> · Lowmeadow LLC` (date = `modified.slice(0, 10)`), author alone when no date. Dated table cell: `<text> (as of <asOf>)`. Glossary: `<li id={term.id}><strong>term</strong>: definition</li>`. Table caption: a `<p>` referenced by the table's `aria-labelledby`. `scripts/publishSiteFiles/renderLearnMarkdown` writes the same strings in the same order (minus the breadcrumb).

17. **Child routes.** Each of the six page folders has its own plan; its `page.tsx` imports its copy module, derives its path as `/learn/${copy.slug}/`, calls `findSitePage(path)` once for metadata (`buildPageMetadata(page)`) and once for render, and renders `<LearnArticle copy page />` plus `<JsonLd document={buildStructuredData({ page, copy })} />`. No literal copy in a route file.

## Cross-module contracts

- Consumes from `src/data/learn`: the roster (six pages in priority order) and each page's copy record (meta, H1, answer/definition, sections with ids, table rows with as-of dates, FAQ items, glossary terms with anchors, related links, draft marker).
- Consumes from `src/app/_shared/listSitePages`: canonical urlPath, `modified`/`published`, `breadcrumb`, `ogImage`, `markdownUrl` per /learn page.
- Consumes `src/app/_shared/buildPageMetadata` for all metadata; `src/service/structuredData` for Article, BreadcrumbList, FAQPage, DefinedTerm; `src/components/JsonLd` to embed.
- Exposes: rendered HTML whose visible FAQ/glossary/breadcrumb text equals the strings handed to the record builders — `tests/seo` and `publishSiteFiles`' markdown copy rely on the same record, not on scraping this HTML.
- Footer `learn` link (root scope) points at `/learn/`.

## Open questions

None open. Resolved 2026-11-27 (decision #43 defaults, applied in plan.aide):
1. Date/author line sits after the answer as a slim learn variant (`LearnByline`, #14, #16), not the DocMeta card.
2. No visible draft notice; the marker stays in the record.
3. Index records: `BreadcrumbList` + `CollectionPage`, no dates (structuredData builds them for `learnIndex`).
4. FAQs: the definition and SDLC pages carry FAQ items (with FAQPage records); the spec-driven page may carry a prose-only FAQ; the other pages carry none (data/learn plan).
5. Column width: the docs layout's 1000px main column and its padding are reused as-is (layout.tsx).
